---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FeatureCard from '../../components/FeatureCard.astro';
import TopicFilter from '../../components/TopicFilter.astro';
import ExploreMore from '../../components/ExploreMore.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
import { fetchAllPublishedCaseStudies } from '../../lib/buildTimeData';
import { caseStudyDetails, caseStudyMonth } from '../../lib/caseStudyDisplay';

const caseStudies = await fetchAllPublishedCaseStudies();
// Same order (and so the same "Case 01" numbering) as the detail pages.
const ordered = caseStudies;
const brandCount = new Set(caseStudies.map((c) => c.category.trim().toLowerCase()).filter(Boolean)).size;
const themeCount = new Set(caseStudies.flatMap((c) => c.tags.map((t) => t.trim().toLowerCase()))).size;
---

<Layout title="Case Studies | Kasturi Lalitha Manogna"
  description="Brand audits and strategy deep dives by Kasturi Lalitha Manogna on how luxury houses like CHANEL build desire at every touchpoint."
>
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head listing-head reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Case Studies &amp; Brand Research</span>
        <h1>Brands I'm Curious About. Questions I'm Trying to Answer.</h1>
        <p>I like looking beyond what a brand is showing us and trying to understand what is happening underneath. Why does this brand feel different? Why does this product have so much meaning? Why does a certain campaign work? Why do consumers keep coming back? And what can another brand learn from it? These projects are my way of exploring those questions.</p>
      </div>

      {caseStudies.length > 0 && (
        <dl class="stat-row reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div><dt>Case studies</dt><dd>{String(caseStudies.length).padStart(2, '0')}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Brands studied</dt><dd>{String(brandCount).padStart(2, '0')}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Themes explored</dt><dd>{String(themeCount).padStart(2, '0')}</dd></div>
        </dl>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="split-aside reveal">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">Method</span>
          <h2>How I Look at a Brand</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split-body reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <ol class="method-steps">
          <li><span class="method-num">01</span><strong>The brand</strong><span>Heritage, codes and what the house stands for.</span></li>
          <li><span class="method-num">02</span><strong>The consumer</strong><span>Who desires it, and why it means something to them.</span></li>
          <li><span class="method-num">03</span><strong>The culture</strong><span>The moment, the generation and the world around it.</span></li>
          <li><span class="method-num">04</span><strong>The strategy</strong><span>Connecting it all back to what the brand should do next.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="method-note">I'm interested in the bigger picture, but I also enjoy getting into the details.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Featured Research</span>
        <h2>The Case Studies</h2>
      </div>

      <TopicFilter itemTags={ordered.map((c) => c.tags)} target="caseStudyList" noun={['case study', 'case studies']} />

      {ordered.length > 0 ? (
        <div class="feature-list" id="caseStudyList">
          {ordered.map((c, i) => (
            <FeatureCard
              href={withBase(`/case-studies/${c.slug}/`)}
              kicker={c.category}
              meta={[caseStudyMonth(c)]}
              number={`Case ${String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}`}
              title={c.title}
              excerpt={c.excerpt}
              tags={c.tags}
              image={c.cover_image ?? c.gallery[0]?.url ?? null}
              ctaLabel={c.coming_soon ? 'Preview case study' : 'Read case study'}
              details={caseStudyDetails(c)}
              badge={c.coming_soon ? 'Coming Soon' : c.featured ? 'Featured' : null}
              badgeTone={c.featured && !c.coming_soon ? 'gold' : 'plain'}
              dataTags={c.tags}
            >
              <div slot="plate" class="brand-plate" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="brand-plate-label">Case Study · {String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                <span class="brand-plate-name">{c.category}</span>
                <span class="brand-plate-rule"></span>
                <span class="brand-plate-foot">{c.tags.slice(0, 3).join(' · ')}</span>
              </div>
            </FeatureCard>
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <p class="journal-status">No case studies published yet — check back soon.</p>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <section class="tight">
    <div class="container split">
      <div class="split-aside reveal">
        <div class="section-head">
          <span class="eyebrow">More to Come</span>
          <h2>This List Is Still Growing</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split-body prose reveal reveal-delay-1">
        <p>I want this section to keep growing. As I work on more brands and marketing problems, I'll keep adding them here.</p>
        <p>The brands I'm studying today are helping me build the kind of strategist I want to become tomorrow.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <ExploreMore current="case-studies" />
</Layout>
